WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:07.791
"If you don't behave," I said to the boy, "I'll take you straight home. Now are you going to be good or not?"

2
00:00:07.792 --> 00:00:15.753
"I was just having a little fun," he said with a pout. "I didn't mean to hurt Old Hank. But what did he hit me for?

3
00:00:15.754 --> 00:00:23.440
I'll behave, Snake-eye, if you don't send me home. And I'll be really good if you'll let me play the Black Scout today."

4
00:00:23.441 --> 00:00:29.892
"I don't know that game," I said. "That's for you and Mr. Bill to decide. He's your playmate for the day.

5
00:00:29.893 --> 00:00:35.174
I'm going away for a while, on business. Now you make friends with Bill right now.

6
00:00:35.175 --> 00:00:39.285
Say you're sorry for hurting him, or you'll go home at once."

7
00:00:39.286 --> 00:00:44.884
Red Chief shook hands with Bill, and then I took my friend outside the cave so we could talk.

8
00:00:44.885 --> 00:00:52.515
"The village of Poplar Cove is three miles from here. I'm going to find out if they've heard anything about the kidnapping," I said.

9
00:00:52.516 --> 00:01:00.378
"Also I think it's best if we send old man Dorset a ransom letter today. We'll demand the money and tell him how to deliver it."

10
00:01:00.379 --> 00:01:06.714
"You know, Sam," Bill said, "I've stood by you during earthquakes without batting an eye.

11
00:01:06.715 --> 00:01:15.572
In fire and flood, I've been shoulder to shoulder with you. In poker games, police raids, train robberies, and cyclones!

12
00:01:15.573 --> 00:01:21.263
I never lost my nerve until we kidnapped that two-legged skyrocket of a kid.

13
00:01:21.264 --> 00:01:25.025
You won't leave me with him a long time, will you, Sam?"

14
00:01:25.026 --> 00:01:27.914
"I'll be back this afternoon," I said.

15
00:01:27.915 --> 00:01:35.864
"Keep the boy amused until I return. I won't be long, I promise. Now let's write the letter to old Dorset."

16
00:01:35.865 --> 00:01:45.026
Bill and I got paper and pencil and worked on the letter while Red Chief, with a blanket wrapped around him, strutted up and down, guarding the mouth of the cave.

17
00:01:45.027 --> 00:01:51.296
"Make the ransom fifteen hundred dollars instead of two thousand," Bill begged with tears in his eyes.

18
00:01:51.297 --> 00:01:57.237
"I'm not questioning a parent's love for a child, but we're dealing with human beings here.

19
00:01:57.238 --> 00:02:04.158
Nobody is going to give up two thousand dollars for that forty-pound devil, that freckled wildcat.

20
00:02:04.159 --> 00:02:08.025
Please, Sam, let's just ask for fifteen hundred dollars."

21
00:02:08.026 --> 00:02:13.810
To make Bill happy, I agreed. We worked together on a letter that read like this:

22
00:02:13.811 --> 00:02:16.191
Dear Mr. Ebenezer Dorset:

23
00:02:16.192 --> 00:02:24.537
We have your boy hidden in a place far from Summit. It is useless for you or the most skillful detectives to attempt to find him.

24
00:02:24.538 --> 00:02:32.684
We will only return him if these conditions are met: we demand fifteen hundred dollars in large bills.

25
00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:39.646
If you agree to these conditions, send your answer by a lone messenger tonight at half-past eight o'clock.

26
00:02:39.647 --> 00:02:52.121
After crossing Owl Creek, and on the road to Poplar Cove, there are three large trees about a hundred yards apart, close to a fence bordering a wheat field on the right-hand side.

27
00:02:52.122 --> 00:02:58.311
At the bottom of the fence post opposite the third tree, there is a small cardboard box.

28
00:02:58.312 --> 00:03:04.668
Your messenger will place your answer and the money in this box and return immediately to Summit.

29
00:03:04.669 --> 00:03:12.807
If you attempt any tricks, or fail to follow our instructions, you will never see your boy again.

30
00:03:12.808 --> 00:03:18.299
If you pay the money, he will be returned safe and well within three hours.

31
00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:25.735
These conditions are final. If you do not accept them, no further communication will be attempted.

32
00:03:25.736 --> 00:03:27.679
TWO DESPERATE MEN

33
00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:34.172
I addressed the letter to Dorset, and put it in my pocket. As I was about to leave, the kid came up to me.

34
00:03:34.173 --> 00:03:40.034
"Aw, Snake-eye, you said I could play the Black Scout while you were gone," the boy said.

35
00:03:40.035 --> 00:03:45.487
"Play it, of course," I said. "Mr. Bill will play with you. What kind of a game is it?"

36
00:03:45.488 --> 00:03:52.418
"I'm the Black Scout," Red Chief said, "and I have to ride to the fort to warn the settlers that the Indians are coming.

37
00:03:52.419 --> 00:03:57.411
I'm tired of playing Indian by myself. I want to be the Black Scout."

38
00:03:57.412 --> 00:04:02.267
"All right," I said. "It sounds harmless to me. Mr. Bill will help you."

39
00:04:02.268 --> 00:04:05.760
"What do I have to do?" Bill asked suspiciously.

40
00:04:05.761 --> 00:04:13.627
"You are the horse," Black Scout said. "Get down on your hands and knees. How can I ride to the fort without a horse?"

41
00:04:13.628 --> 00:04:19.750
"You better keep him interested, Bill," I said, "until we get this scheme going. Loosen up."

42
00:04:19.751 --> 00:04:26.250
Bill got down on all fours, and a look came into his eyes like a rabbit gets when it's caught in a trap.

43
00:04:26.251 --> 00:04:30.364
"How far is it to the fort, kid?" he croaked.

44
00:04:30.365 --> 00:04:37.167
"Ninety miles," the Black Scout said, "and you have to gallop hard to get there on time."

45
00:04:37.168 --> 00:04:41.578
The Black Scout jumped on Bill's back and dug his heels into his sides.

46
00:04:41.579 --> 00:04:50.816
"For heaven's sake, Sam," Bill said, "hurry back as soon as you can. I wish we hadn't made the ransom more than a thousand."

47
00:04:50.817 --> 00:04:57.315
Then Bill turned to Red Chief—excuse me—Black Scout, who was still sitting on his back.

48
00:04:57.316 --> 00:05:02.140
"Quit kicking me," shouted Bill, "or I'll get up and spank you hard!"

49
00:05:02.141 --> 00:05:08.925
I walked over to Poplar Cove and sat around the post office and store, talking with the country hicks that came in.

50
00:05:08.926 --> 00:05:19.663
One old farmer said, "I hear Summit is all upset about Ebenezer Dorset's boy being lost or stolen."

51
00:05:19.664 --> 00:05:24.063
"What great news!" I thought as I bought some soda.

52
00:05:24.064 --> 00:05:32.140
To look casual, I remarked to no one in particular, "The price of black-eyed peas seems a bit high this season."

53
00:05:32.141 --> 00:05:36.250
Then I dropped my letter into the mail slot when no one was looking.

54
00:05:36.251 --> 00:05:43.268
As I walked away, I overheard the postmaster telling a customer that the mail would go out to Summit in one hour.

55
00:05:43.269 --> 00:05:47.021
When I got back to the cave, I could not find Bill and the boy.

56
00:05:47.022 --> 00:05:54.336
I explored the entire cave and the surrounding area and risked a yodel or two, but there was no response.

57
00:05:54.344 --> 00:05:59.579
So I lit my pipe and sat down on a mossy bank to see what would happen next.

